  "package": "odm",
  "source": "CCSDS 502.0-B-3 annex G",
  "note": "Orbit Data Messages. These are ASCII files rather than octet strings, so the two worked examples annex G prints are shipped as readable .kvn files under corpus and also carried here as decode vectors, hex-encoded because that is the only form the schema has for an input. A consumer can use either. What the decode vectors assert is the text and integer content: the version, the originator, the object identifiers, the frames, the epoch and the number of maneuvers. The numeric state vector is not asserted here, because a vector field has no float accessor and pinning floats as formatted strings would test this package's chosen number formatting rather than the standard. Those values are checked in pkg/odm against the same published text. Only the OPM is covered; the OMM, OEM and OCM are not implemented yet.",
  "corpus": [
    "odm/opm-simple.kvn",
    "odm/opm-maneuvers.kvn"
  ],
  "decode": [
